Guard the one WIN32_APP call that upstream left unguarded.

i2pd's Win32/DaemonWin32.cpp guards every other use of the i2p::win32 namespace
behind #ifdef WIN32_APP (lines 18, 66, 84, 92) but misses the one in
GetGracefulShutdownInterval. Building with USE_WIN32_APP=no therefore fails:

  Win32/DaemonWin32.cpp:104:29: error: 'i2p::win32' has not been declared

gipny needs USE_WIN32_APP=no because the bundled router is a background child
process driven over SAM. With WIN32_APP the daemon registers a tray icon
unconditionally (Win32/Win32App.cpp:99, Shell_NotifyIcon(NIM_ADD)) with no flag
to suppress it, so a stray i2pd tray icon would appear next to the app.

Reported upstream; carried here rather than in a fork so it is visible in review
(see third_party/README.md).

--- a/Win32/DaemonWin32.cpp
+++ b/Win32/DaemonWin32.cpp
@@ -101,7 +101,11 @@
 
 	int DaemonWin32::GetGracefulShutdownInterval () const
 	{
+#ifdef WIN32_APP
 		return i2p::win32::GetGracefulShutdownRemainingTime ();
+#else
+		return 0;
+#endif
 	}	
 }
 }
